  "description": "The \u0027dss_plugins_live\u0027 dataset provides comprehensive information about various plugins available in a live environment. Each entry in the dataset represents a unique plugin, identified by a unique ID and a human-readable label. The dataset includes details such as the version number, which helps track updates and changes, and the author, providing information about the creator or contributors. Tags are used to categorize plugins, making it easier to search and filter them based on specific keywords. A detailed description of each plugin\u0027s functionality and use cases is provided, offering insights into how the plugin can be utilized. The dataset also indicates whether a plugin is still in development, which is crucial for understanding its current status. Additionally, a URL is provided for each plugin, linking to a summary page for more detailed information. This dataset is particularly useful for developers, project managers, and users who need to manage and utilize plugins effectively in their projects.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of live plugins with details on version, author, and status.",
